  "critique": {
   "status": "done",
   "result": {
    "critique": "The base results are negative in both train and validation, and the validation sample is tiny (n=34, 12 blocks). The validation confidence interval barely crosses zero, but the median is still about -49%, so the central outcome is strongly negative and any positive upper bound is probably noise. The strategy underperforms the unconditional baseline in both periods, meaning the earnings-within-10d condition appears to worsen a losing straddle rather than add edge. Cost realism fails because all validation trades were earnings-event trades and the stricter lower bound is about -42%, so executable costs would make it worse. Tail risk is severe, with near-total single-trade losses and multi-hundred-percent 10-day windows. Reuse of the same validation window and many likely variants raises overfitting concerns.",
    "doubts": [
     "Validation N=34 and only 12 blocks; CI includes zero/positive but median -48.7%, so no reliable edge.",
     "Underperforms the no-condition baseline in both train and validation, suggesting the condition adds no value.",
     "Cost realism failed because all validation trades were earnings-event trades and stricter lower bound was -42%.",
     "Worst trade -99.9% and worst window -631% show ruinous tail risk for a long straddle.",
     "Train had 107 stale implied vol drops; this may bias the surviving sample.",
     "Same validation window reused and many variants tested creates multiple-testing/overfitting risk.",
     "No specific strike selection, option pricing/greeks, or bid-ask spread modeling was tested, so results may not reflect executable straddles."
